WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.800
Movie Mission Life on Mars. Beyond the confines of our blue planet lies a world cloaked in mystery and intrigue a

00:08.160 --> 00:14.540
Silent sentinel in the vast expanse of the cosmos a red jewel that has captured the human imagination for eons

00:14.960 --> 00:18.400
Mars an average of 140 million miles

00:18.840 --> 00:24.320
Separates us from this enigmatic neighbor a journey of epic proportions even at the speed of light

00:24.920 --> 00:29.640
Yet it's not just the distance that fascinates us, but what lies beneath its reddish hue

00:30.280 --> 00:34.480
This crimson facade is the result of iron oxide or rust

00:35.040 --> 00:39.100
Painting the Martian surface earning at the moniker the red planet

00:39.440 --> 00:43.680
But this color this rust is more than a mere cosmetic feature

00:43.800 --> 00:49.640
It's a clue a hint at the geological processes that have shaped the Martian landscape over billions of years

00:50.160 --> 00:57.840
Mars a celestial body of iron oxide and mysteries beckons us to uncover its secrets as we traverse the cosmic expanse

00:57.960 --> 01:05.080
We encounter a landscape unlike any other welcome to Mars a planet of stark contrasts and captivating topography

01:05.080 --> 01:12.600
It's surface a rich tapestry of geological wonders tells a tale of the planet's tumultuous past and offers clues to its future

01:13.320 --> 01:16.440
Let's take a closer look at some of these marvels first

01:16.440 --> 01:21.080
We have Olympus Mons a behemoth that dwarfs every mountain and volcano

01:22.040 --> 01:28.400
This shield volcano the largest in our solar system soars nearly 14 miles into the Martian sky a

01:28.760 --> 01:33.440
Testament to the planet's volcanic activity, but Mars isn't just about towering heights

01:33.600 --> 01:40.120
It also boasts of profound depths enter Valles Marineris a Grand Canyon system that stretches over

01:40.480 --> 01:45.240
2,500 miles across the Martian surface almost 10 times longer than our Grand Canyon and

01:45.480 --> 01:47.480
Reaches depths of up to four miles

01:47.720 --> 01:55.500
This vast chasm believed to have formed as the planet cooled and contracted is a magnificent display of Mars's tectonic forces at play

01:55.800 --> 01:59.600
Mars a world of red dust is more than just a barren desert

01:59.600 --> 02:06.960
It's a planet adorned by towering peaks and deep canyons each carrying their own unique story of Mars's geological history

02:07.120 --> 02:14.560
It's a landscape shaped by time by forces both violent and slow a testament to the power of nature at a planetary scale a

02:14.800 --> 02:19.960
Terrain of extremes Mars offers an unparalleled vista of towering peaks and deep canyons

02:20.520 --> 02:28.000
Above the rugged landscape a thin cold blanket of air envelops the Martian world. This is no ordinary atmosphere

02:28.000 --> 02:34.840
It's one almost entirely composed of carbon dioxide a stark contrast to the oxygen rich air. We breathe here on earth

02:35.440 --> 02:41.800
95% of it is carbon dioxide in fact with mere traces of nitrogen and argon making up the rest now

02:41.800 --> 02:44.080
Let's talk temperatures Mars isn't a place

02:44.080 --> 02:48.240
You'd want to visit without a heavy-duty spacesuit in the depths of a Martian winter

02:48.680 --> 02:52.040
Temperatures at the poles can plummet to a bone-chilling negative

02:52.800 --> 02:57.880
195 degrees Fahrenheit that's colder than the coldest temperature ever recorded on earth

02:58.480 --> 03:03.740
But it's not all icy desolation near the Martian equator in the peak of a summer day

03:04.160 --> 03:08.280
Temperatures can actually climb to a relatively balmy 70 degrees Fahrenheit

03:08.480 --> 03:12.960
That's a temperature swing more extreme than anything we experience here on our home planet

03:13.200 --> 03:20.160
However, despite these harsh conditions Mars continues to captivate us with its alien beauty and the potential secrets

03:20.160 --> 03:22.160
It holds its thin cold

03:22.440 --> 03:27.520
Atmosphere while vastly different from our own is an integral part of what makes this red planet

03:27.520 --> 03:34.760
So intriguing the Martian atmosphere harsh and unyielding stands as a stark reminder of the planet's inhospitable nature

03:35.080 --> 03:39.200
Yet it is this very characteristic that fuels our curiosity

03:39.520 --> 03:43.300
Spurring us onward in our quest to unravel the mysteries of the cosmos

03:43.760 --> 03:50.120
Amidst the harsh realities of Mars a glimmer of hope persists as we delve deeper into the red planet's secrets

03:50.120 --> 03:56.160
We uncover compelling hints of life's potential beneath the Martian surface vast reserves of water

03:56.160 --> 04:01.640
I sleep silently hinting at a past that was perhaps not so barren in the distant past

04:02.000 --> 04:05.640
Liquid water may have flowed freely shaping the Martian landscapes

04:05.640 --> 04:11.840
We see today could these waters have been a cradle for life much like our own earth our curiosity fuels

04:12.080 --> 04:17.480
Relentless exploration as we send mission after mission each one armed with the latest technology

04:17.880 --> 04:23.900
Probing the Martian terrain for traces of microbial life the faintest whiff of biological activity

04:23.920 --> 04:29.280
The smallest trace of a past or present microbe could change our understanding of life itself

04:29.280 --> 04:36.180
It would prove that we are not alone in this vast cosmos the quest for life on Mars continues fueling our cosmic

04:36.400 --> 04:38.400
curiosity and the spirit of exploration

